The description given for that bash command was **"Extract per-turn input distributions"**.

The full command (recorded in the "diagnosis (2)" phase, seq 264) was:

```
node -e "
const fs = require('fs');
const all = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/private/tmp/claude-501/.../scratchpad/all-runs.json','utf8'));
const inputs = (label, arm) => all.perRun.filter(r => r.label===label && r.arm===arm).flatMap(r => r.turns.map(t => t.usage.input));
console.log('CT5='+JSON.stringify(inputs('iter5','context-tree')));
console.log('CT6='+JSON.stringify(inputs('iter6','context-tree')));
"
```

It pulled the per-turn `usage.input` tokens for the context-tree arm from iter5 (CT5) and iter6 (CT6) out of `all-runs.json` — data that fed the O(trace)→O(delta) fresh-input finding.
